<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mrauk U</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mrohaung</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mrauk U is a town in Rakhine State, western Myanmar, that was the capital of the Arakanese kingdom from 1430 to 1785. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/min-saw-mon">Min Saw Mon</a> after he regained his throne with help from the Bengal Sultanate, it grew rich on trade across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a> and was visited by Portuguese, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and other merchants. Its many stone temples and pagodas survive as an archaeological site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mrauk-u.jpg" alt="Mrauk U" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jmhullot · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MysticalMraukU.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
